SUNAGAKURE WIND-USER ORDNANCE -- GIANT FOLDING FAN REGISTRY

Purpose: To track the great folding battle fans (tessen) entrusted to
qualified wind-nature shinobi of the Hidden Sand. The fan is both signal
device and offensive instrument; each is marked with the purple moons
denoting the bearer's mastery.

Registered bearers of record:
- Temari of the Sand Siblings -- three-moon war fan, primary carrier.
  Cleared for Wind Release: Great Sickle Weasel Technique and cooperative
  scythe-weasel summoning. Fan calibrated for gale-force cutting winds.
- Reserve jonin (2) -- two-moon training fans, drill use only.

Handling doctrine: The fan is never to be opened in confined tunnels of the
village interior. Full extension exposes all three moons and commits the
bearer to maximum output. Damaged ribs must be reforged by the Workshop, as
a warped fan disperses chakra unevenly and endangers allied formations.
Authorization: Kazekage Office, Wind Division.
